Let's break this problem down step by step. First, an iron pickaxe allows a dwarf to mine twice as much as bare hands, so they mine 12 * 2 = 24 pounds per day. Next, a steel pickaxe allows a dwarf to mine 50% more than with an iron pickaxe, so they mine 24 + (24 * 0.50) = 24 + 12 = 36 pounds per day.  With steel pickaxes, 40 dwarves can mine 40 * 36 = 1440 pounds of ore per day. Over a month with 30 days, they can mine 1440 * 30 = 43200 pounds of ore.  Therefore, 40 dwarves with steel pickaxes can mine 43200 pounds of ore in a month.

\boxed{43200}

